id: pm-vcs-forgeleaseexpiry
title: Prevent served CLI fixture leases expiring during concurrent npm test
description: The unchanged installed served-forge CLI fixture in test/served-forge.test.ts acquires a 60000 ms publication lease and reuses it for a final push after many real CLI processes. A full Node-only npm test run failed with lease_expired after 86 seconds; the same test passed in both serial release gates (49 and 27 seconds) and in a focused Node-only rerun. Keep production expiry checks and explicit short-lease refusal tests intact; make this non-expiry fixture renew at publication or use a lifetime covering its execution budget.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-16T00:29:19.786Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T00:48:25.652Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Default concurrent npm test remains reliable under host contention without bypassing production lease expiry enforcement; Retain real installed CLI and HTTP coverage and explicit expiry refusal regressions
parent: pm-vcs-5h6j
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T00:48:18.128Z",codex-agent,"Evidence: the initial full default-concurrency Node-only npm test had 1549 passed, 1 failed, 4 expected Bun skips; installed served-forge CLI failed its final push with lease_expired after 86.364 seconds. This test and its lease fixture are unchanged from main. It passed in both serial release gates (48.649 and 27.070 seconds), a focused Node-only rerun (1/1), and the unchanged full Node-only retry (57.810 seconds; 1550 passed, 0 failed, 4 Bun skips). No production lease check, test assertion, timeout or fixture lifetime was changed. Keep this follow-up open for deterministic fixture renewal or lifetime handling under contention."
  "2026-10-19T00:41:38.576Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced during PR #126 certification on source 87e0b0049d5506f3d792c6236701cca6a2a9ffcf: npm release gate completed 1634/1635 tests, with only the unchanged installed served-forge CLI scenario failing its final push with lease_expired after 84.517 seconds. git diff origin/main -- test/served-forge.test.ts is empty. The same full Bun release gate passed 1635/1635 with all 67 production files at 100%. Reusing this existing issue. The fixture acquires 60000 ms while its existing scenario timeout is 180000 ms. Plan: share the existing 180000 ms budget between the scenario timeout and this non-expiry fixture lease. No production lease duration, validation, explicit 1 ms expiry test, assertion or test timeout will change. Prove the boundary with a real delayed installed-CLI scenario and only the fixture lifetime reverted; then refresh the required gates."
  "2026-10-19T00:48:25.652Z",codex-agent,"Controlled behavioral proof uses the existing installed-CLI/real-HTTP scenario in an isolated source copy, rebuilt compiled extension bytes, and an added 65-second delay before its final push. With the shared existing 180000 ms fixture budget as lease lifetime: 1/1 pass, exit 0, scenario 124.401 seconds. Revert only that acquisition lifetime to 60000 ms: 0/1 pass, exit 1, final push returns lease_expired. Both retain the unchanged 180000 ms test timeout and every original assertion; no SDK mocks or production lease edits. Normal linked acceptance via pm test pm-vcs-forgeleaseexpiry --run --only-last --progress passes 1/1, exit 0. Build:test and lint pass. Explicit 1 ms expired-grant refusal coverage remains unchanged. The fixture lifetime now covers its allowed execution budget instead of silently relying on fast CLI startups."
